From 88ad2fd281fb7cd5b2c04d9d05c10a8b171932cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Philip B. Krogh" <71797726+phibkro@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:24:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] XOpenDevice: retain the requested ID across the reply wait

_XReply can release the display lock while waiting for the server.
Another thread can then reuse the output request buffer before
XOpenDevice reads req->deviceid. Preserve the caller-supplied ID instead
of reading the potentially overwritten request.

A two-thread Xvfb test requests a valid pointer while a second thread
sends XNoOp requests on the same display. Three unpatched libXi 1.8.4
runs returned device 127 for requested device 4. With this change, three
runs completed 50000 open/map/close cycles each without an ID mismatch.
No devices are removed and no input events are injected.
---
 src/XOpenDev.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/XOpenDev.c b/src/XOpenDev.c
index 4b3c460..0859825 100644
--- a/src/XOpenDev.c
+++ b/src/XOpenDev.c
@@ -99,7 +99,7 @@ XOpenDevice(
     if (dev) {
 	int dlen;	/* data length */
 
-	dev->device_id = req->deviceid;
+	dev->device_id = id;
 	dev->num_classes = rep.num_classes;
 	dev->classes = (XInputClassInfo *) ((char *)dev + sizeof(XDevice));
 	dlen = rep.num_classes * sizeof(xInputClassInfo);
-- 
2.55.0

